$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of F1 Hexanedioic acid (0.146 g, 1.00 mmol), b (0.260 g, 2.17
mmol, 8.5% excess) and d (0.280 g, 2.30 mmol, 15% excess) and THF (1 mL)
were mixed and heated to 40 °C with stirring in a 25mL Schlenk flask. The
reaction mixture was precipitated into cold diethyl ether (4 °C) after
stirring for 48 h, and a brown viscous liquid after being dried under
vacuum. A small amount of this compound (0.050 g) was further purified by
silica gel column chromatography (ethyl acetate), and 0.045 g was
obtained. The impurity was compound b as confirmed by thin layer
chromatography. This purified compound is designated as F1'. White solid,
yield (0.531 g, 84%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini reaction, Schlenk flask used
