0.50 mmol, 1.0 equiv), phenyl acetic acid (9) (71 mg, 0.525 mmol, 1.05
equiv), aldehyde 10 (50 mg, 58 μL, 0.525 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and 20 mol %
of catalyst 4 in CH2Cl2was stirred for 21 hrs. After removal of solvent
followed by silica gel chromatography, 16 (145 mg, 83%) was obtained as a
white solid. Data for 16: 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.42 -7.35(dd,J =
0.8, 2.0 Hz, 2H, aryl); 7.36-7.28 (m, 6H, aryl); 7.26 (s,1 H, furyl);
7.18-7.16 (m, 2H, aryl); 6.49 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H, furyl); 6.37-6.36 (dd,
J = 2.0, 3.2 Hz, 1H, furyl); 6.27 (s, 1H, CH); 6.19 (bt, 1H, NH);
4.44-4.39 (dd, J = 6.0, 14.8 Hz, 1H, CH2-NH); 4.35-4.30 (dd, J = 6.0,
14.8 Hz, 1H, CH2-NH); 3.70 (s, 2H, CH2). 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
169.6, 166.1, 148.0, 143.8, 137.6, 133.4, 129.3, 129.0, 127.9, 127.7,
11.8, 110.9, 69.0, 43.6, 41.5 TLC:. Rf 0.37 (Ethyl Acetate:Hexanes, 1:2)
LRMS LC/EIMS calculated for C21H19NO4+ [M+ H]+: 350.1, found: 349.7 HPLC:
(+/−)-16 tR13.78 min (50.7%); tR 21.42 min (49.3 %) (−)-16 tR14.95 min
(18.8%); tR 22.13 min (81.2%) (Daicel Chiralpak AS OR: 0.46 cm φ x 25 cm,
5% IPA in Hexane, 1 mL/min; isocratic) [α]D22= -12.2° (CHCl3, c = 1.02)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, molecular sieves used in second stage, molecular sieves
used in third stage, Passerini reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
