$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Passerini 3CR: The aldehyde (0.125 mmol, 1eq.),
Isocyanide (0.25 mmol, 2eq.) and carboxylic acid (0.125 mmol, 1eq.) were
added to 125 μL of the solvent in a 1/2 dram glass vial and stirred
overnight. After removal of solvent in vacuo, the reaction products were
purified by flash column chromatography. In reactions where an alcohol
was included, 2eq. of the alcohol were added along with the substrates at
the beginning of the reaction. 1a1 (Table 1) Flash Chromatography
conditions: CH2Cl2 until isocyanide and aldehyde eluted then 20:1
(CH2Cl2: ethyl acetate). 1H NMR (400MHz; CDCl3): δ 8.23 (d, J = 8.8, 2H),
7.65 (d, J = 8.8, 2H), 7.38-7.32 (m, 3H), 7.25 (d, J = 5, 2H), 6.71 (br,
1H), 6.23 (s, 1H), 5.83-5.74 (m, 1H), 5.06-5.95 (m, 2H), 4.48 (d, J =
5.8, 2H), 2.60 (td, J = 7.26, 2.76, 2H), 2.42 (q, J = 6.9, 2H). 13C NMR
(100MHz; CDCl3): δ 170.9, 167.0, 148.1, 142.5, 137.3, 136.1, 128.9,
128.1, 127.9, 127.8, 123.9, 116.2, 74.4, 43.5, 33.3, 28.6. LRMS: calcd
368.38 for C20H20N2O5, observed 391.5 [M + Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bronsted Acidity of Substrates Influences the Outcome of Passerini
Three-Component Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Okandeji, Babajide O.; Sello, Jason K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(14), 5067-5070

