$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The Passerini reaction of acid 1 in water
gives the product in quantitative yield after 30 min under
ultrasonication. Ethyl
2-(4-methyl-2-(2-methyl-4-oxoazetidin-1-yl)pentanamido)acetate (14).
Isolated as a 1:1 mixture of diastereomers. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.04 (m,
1H), 4.17 (q, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 4.01-4.07 (m, 1H), 3.93-4.00 (m, 2H),
3.72-3.84 (m, 1H), 3.07 (dt, J = 11.1 Hz, 3.9 Hz, 1H), 2.52 (m, 1H),
1.55-1.86 (m, 3H), 1.35 (m, 3H), 1.25 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 3H), 0.90-0.95 (m,
6H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 171.3, 171.1, 169.6, 168.2, 168.1, 61.5, 60.5,
56.5, 55.4, 49.3, 48.0, 43.7, 41.4, 41.3, 39.2, 37.6, 25.1, 25.0, 22.8,
22.7, 22.0, 21.8, 19.9, 19.3, 14.3, 14.2. IR (neat): 3318, 2959, 2872,
2249, 1732, 1673, 1532, 1469, 1377, 1351, 1194, 1099, 1070, 1026, 919,
864, 729 cm-1. HRMS (ESI), calcd for C14H25N2O4 [M+H]+ 285.1808, found
285.1813
