$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of α-acyloxy-α-cyanoamide 5a: A
homogeneous mixture of pyruvonitrile (4.4 mmol) and acetic acid (4.4
mmol) was stirred for 10 min at 0°C under argon, then cyclohexyl
isonitrile (4 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was warmed to rt and
stirred for 1 h, whereupon any volatile residues were removed in vacuo
(0.1 Torr, 4 h). The crude product was purified by crystallization from
EtOH to afford white needles of 5a (0.57 g, 68%): 5t: The crude product
was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (3:7
EtOAc/hexanes, Rf = 0.28) to afford a white solid (0.56 g, 82%): mp 54-56
°C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.42 (s, 1 H), 3.4-3.6 (m, 4 H), 3.36 (s, 3 H), 2.44
(dt, 2 H, J = 1.9, 7.5 Hz), 1.67 (p, 2 H, J = 7.4 Hz), 1.2-1.4 (m, 8 H),
1.19 (s, 9 H), 0.87 (t, 3 H, J = 6.8 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 171.76,
162.35, 116.16, 80.22, 70.47, 58.79, 40.00, 38.37, 33.65, 31.55, 28.86,
28.82, 25.22, 24.50, 22.54, 14.02 ppm; IR (neat) 3367 (m), 2931 (s), 2857
(s), 1758 (s), 1693 (s), 1527 (s), 1110 (m), 1022 (m) cm-1; CIMS
(methane) m/z: 341 (M+H), 239, 215, 188, 127.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent, Passerini condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Three-Component Condensation Leading to β-Amino Acid Diamides: Convergent
Assembly of β-Peptide Analogues
