$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Isocyanide 3 (3.3 mmol) was added to the
suspension of the carboxylic acid 2 (3.3 mmol) and the aldehyde 1 (3.0
mmol) at room temperature. The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient
temperature for 24 h and then concentrated in vacuo. The crude product
was purified by crystallization from ethyl octane/ hexane to afford the
corresponding product 4. Compound 4c, yield 82%. mp 101-103 °C. 1H NMR
(200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.26 (t, J= 7.1 Hz, 3H), 4.08 (dd, J= 5.3 Hz; J=
7.1 Hz, 2H), 4.21 (q, J= 7.1 Hz, 2H), 6.39 (s. 1H), 6.80 (s, 1H),
7.25-8.14 (m, 10H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.4. 41.6, 62.0, 76.1.
127.8, 128.9, 129.1, 129.4, 130.1, 134.0, 135.6, 165.3, 168.7, 169.7.
Anal, calcd. for C19H19NO5: C, 66.85; H, 5.61; N, 4.10. Found: C, 66.61;
H, 5.82; N, 4.11. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C19H19NO5Na [M + Na]+:
364.1160. Found: 364.1 155.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Passerini reaction, reaction run in solvent gave lower
yield, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solvent-free Passerini reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
