$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Phenol-Induced Ugi-4CR.
To a 1 M solution of the aldehyde (1 mmol) in methanol was added
successively 1.0 equiv of amine, 1.0 equiv of isocyanide, and 1.0 equiv
of phenol under inert atmosphere. The resulting mixture was stirred until
completion (TLC). It was then concentrated in vacuo, and the crude
product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel. 2-[(4-Chloro
benzyl)-(2-nitro phenyl)amino]-2-(4-chloro phenyl)-N-cyclohexyl
acetamide:Yellow solid. Yield (20h at 60°C in MeOH): 80%. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz) δ 7.67 (dd, 1H, J = 8.1, 1.5 Hz), 7.47-7.33 (m, 4H), 7.28-7.22
(m, 2H), 7.18-7.12 (m, 3H), 6.96 (d, 1H, J = 7.1 Hz), 6.65 (d, 2H, J =
8.1 Hz), 4.80 (s, 1H), 4.01 (d, 1H, J = 14.1 Hz), 3.95 (d, 1H, J = 14.1
Hz), 3.53-3.46 (m, 1H), 1.72-1.50 (m, 4H), 1.45-1.25 (m, 4H), 1.15-1.04
(m, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ 169.8, 147.8, 141.9, 135.0, 134.8,
134.4, 132.9, 133.0, 131.2, 130.3, 129.3, 128.9, 127.3, 126.1, 124.9,
71.2, 57.0, 48.2, 32.8, 25.7, 24.9, 22.7. IR (thin film) 3332, 2929,
2854, 1662, 1522, 1364, 1090, 1015 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 513. Anal.
Calcd for C27H27Cl2N3O3: C, 63.28 ; H, 5.31. Found: C, 63.24 ; H, 5.56.
m.p. 156°C.
