$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Passerini 3CR: The
aldehyde (0.125 mmol, 1eq.), Isocyanide (0.25 mmol, 2eq.) and carboxylic
acid (0.125 mmol, 1eq.) were added to 125 μL of the solvent in a 1/2 dram
glass vial and stirred overnight. After removal of solvent in vacuo, the
reaction products were purified by flash column chromatography. In
reactions where an alcohol was included, 2eq. of the alcohol were added
along with the substrates at the beginning of the reaction. 1b (Table 1)
Flash Chromatography conditions: CH2Cl2 until isocyanide and aldehyde
eluted then 20:1 (CH2Cl2: ethyl acetate). 1H NMR (400MHz; CDCl3): δ 8.23
(d, J = 8.9, 2H), 7.68 (d, J = 8.7, 2H), 7.36-7.31 (m, 3H), 7.26-7.17 (m,
3H), 6.77 (br, 1H), 6.29 (s, 1H), 5.96 (dt, J = 15.7, 1.7, 1H), 4.50 (dd,
J = 5.8, 3.0, 2H), 2.33-2.26 (m, 2H), 1.1 (t, J = 7.4, 3H). 13C NMR
(100MHz; CDCl3): δ 167.3, 164.5, 154.5, 148.0, 145.8, 142.8, 137.4,
128.9, 128.0, 127.9, 127.7, 123.8, 118.5, 74.1, 43.5, 25.6, 11.9. HRMS:
calcd 391.1270 for C20H20N2NaO5 ([M + Na]+), observed 391.1280.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bronsted Acidity of Substrates Influences the Outcome of Passerini
Three-Component Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Okandeji, Babajide O.; Sello, Jason K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(14), 5067-5070

