$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Acyloxy-3-chlorocarboxamides 4; General
Procedure: α-Chloro ketone 1 (10 mmol) is added dropwise over 15 min to
an ice-cooled mixture of carboxylic acid 2 (10 mmol) and isocyanide 3 (10
mmol). The mixture is stirred for 15 h at room temperature. The resulting
product is purified by distillation or by crystallisation from petroleum
ether. 2-Acyloxy-3-chloropropanamide 4c. Yield: 78%. m.p.: 46 [°C],
Molecular Formula: C10H18ClNO3 (235.7). Microanalyses: C, ± 0.23; H, ±
0.19; N, ± 0.47: Cl, ± 0.40. I.R. (Nujol) ν[cm-1]: 1680; 1746; 3425.
1H-N.M.R. (CDCl3/TMSint) δ [ppm]: 1.40 (s, 9H); 1.67 (s, 3 H); 2.15 (s,
3H); 4.26. 4.05 (νA, νB, 2H, JAB = 11.2 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A convenient conversion of 2-acyloxy-3-chlorocarboxamides to
3-acyloxy-2-azetidinones in heterogeneous media
