$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Aminopyrimidine or
Aminopyridine Derivative Synthesis. To a 1 M solution of carbonyl
compound (1 mmol) in methanol or toluene were added the amine (1.0
equiv), the isocyanide (1.0 equiv), and the hydroxypyrimidine or
hydroxypyridine (1.0 equiv). The resulting mixture was stirred at 60 or
90 °C under an inert atmosphere and concentrated in vacuo. The crude
product was then purified by flash chromatography on silica gel to give
the desired adduct.
2-(N-(4-Chlorobenzyl)-N-(2,6-dimethylpyrimidin-4-yl)amino)-
N-cyclohexylbutanamide (Table 5, entry 2): colorless oil; yield (72 h at
60 °C in MeOH) 78%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.28 (d, 2H, J = 8.3 Hz),
7.13 (d, 2H, J = 8.3 Hz), 6.71 (br s, 1H), 5.95 (s, 1H), 5.12 (br s,1H),
4.72 (d, 1H, J = 17.9 Hz), 4.52 (d, 1H, J = 17.9 Hz), 3.75-3.65 (m, 1H),
2.56 (s, 3H), 2.26 (s, 3H), 2.13-1.99 (m, 2H), 1.93-1.83 (m, 1H),
1.73-1.49 (m, 4H), 1.46- 1.06 (m, 5H), 0.90 (t, 3H, J = 7.3 Hz); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ 170.1, 166.6, 166.3, 163.2, 136.7, 133.2, 129.3,
128.0, 100.7, 59.8, 48.6, 48.1, 33.4, 33.1, 26.6, 25.9, 24.9, 24.8, 24.7,
22.3, 11.4; IR (thin film) 3338, 2940, 2856, 1680, 1596, 1489, 1355, 1282
cm-1; MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 415; HRMS calcd for C23H31- ClN4O 414.2186,
found 414.2179.
