$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Formation of
Phosphonate 5: To acyl chloride 1 (2 mmol) was added neat trialkyl
phosphite (1 equiv). The mixture was stirred under argon for 30 min.
Toluene (1 M), isocyanide (1 equiv) and carboxylic acid (1 equiv) were
then successively added. The mixture was stirred for 24 h under argon at
r.t. (for alkyl acyl chlorides) or at 80 °C (for aromatic acyl
chlorides). The solvent was then removed under reduced pressure to afford
Passerini products after purification by flash column chromatography on
silica gel. Compound 5i, yield 78a %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini reaction, neat reactants 1st stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Isocyanide addition to acylphosphonates: a formal Passerini reaction of
acyl chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
