$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of Ugi products for Pyrrolidinones
and Pyridones: To 1 mmol aldehyde in 2 mL MeOH, 1 mmol amine is added and
it is stirred for 5 min. Then, 1 eq pyridinium hydrochloride is added in
case of sodium salt of β -keto aldehydes. After that, 1 mmol phosphono
acetic acid and 1 mmol isocyanide are added. The reaction mixture is
stirred for a night at room temperature. For the work up, the solvent is
evaporated and 3 mL DCM and 2 mL water are added. The aqueous layer is
extracted with 1 mL DCM. The organic layers are combined and washed twice
with 2 mL citric acid (5%), sat. NaHCO3 solution and brine. The organic
layer was dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuum. The product could
be crystallized or otherwise purified by column or wave chromatography or
preparative HPLC.
{[Benzyl-(1-cyclohexylcarbamoyl-2-hydroxy-2-phenyl-vinyl)-carbamoyl]-methyl}-phosphonic
acid diethyl ester (1): scheduled quantity 3 mmol gave 1204 mg (76%)
C28H37N2O6P MW: 528.59 g/mol; HPLC-MS (ESI): tR = 3.86 min, m/z = 529
[M+H]+, 551 [M+Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Ugi reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Substituted Pyrrolidinones and Pyridones by 4-CR/2-CR Sequence
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
